         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Number Families\n\nSo far, we have seen how we can relate the life of parents to their children through numbers with units and tens.\n\nBut in life, we need to count much more than 99 quantities.\n\nIn this lesson, we will expand on this knowledge.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "7506de0c-bc97-4263-b5cf-75f9a477e6ce",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "7506de0c-bc97-4263-b5cf-75f9a477e6ce",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "To use numbers greater than 99, would it be enough to start a new number family — order — starting at 100 and going up to 199, then 200 to 299, and so on?",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown/html/text",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "7b7eda12-2ca9-45f9-a85a-b0f9eb3a0726",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": "yes",
         "score": 2,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "7b7eda12-2ca9-45f9-a85a-b0f9eb3a0726",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Logic\n\nThe change from one number family to the next — order — always happens the same way when we work with numbers. Whenever all the previous orders reach 9, the next digit increases by one and the previous ones go back to zero.\n\nLet us see some examples:\n\n- After 99 we have 100\n- After 999 we have 1000\n- After 9,999 we have 10,000\n\nAnd so on.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "5ed5b836-933d-4f53-83dc-97d1db090106",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "5ed5b836-933d-4f53-83dc-97d1db090106",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "We have already said that numbers have their generations — orders — which we call units and tens. Do the other orders also have names?",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "41e9922f-cb01-40b5-a2e1-54052ca249d2",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 2,
         "position": ""
      },
